      {
        "id": 54526,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-13T22:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>&nbsp;You do raise an interesting point about Mr. Fixer though.&nbsp;&nbsp; I suppose in order to stay consistent I would be obligated to say:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Fixer Uses Strike to deal 1 damage to Baron Blade, but he has Crowbars so he deals 2 damage.&nbsp;&nbsp; Fixer deals the same amount of damage (2 damage) to Blade Batallion, but he has crowbars, so he deals 3 damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This would mean the offhand attack is always stronger than the original strike.&nbsp;&nbsp; And if Monkey Fist were also in play the damage on the attacks would be 3/5. &nbsp; If you tack on Harmony you're up to 4/7.&nbsp; I have never played it this way before,&nbsp; but the wording on the card does indeed seem to indicate it would be the case.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
