      {
        "id": 54528,
        "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
        "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-13T23:18:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There's a thread with a second-hand Christopher response stating that Dual Crowbars don't get to double dip on damage boosts; the \"same amount\" wording is meant to denote that.</p><p>The difference here is Sacrosanct Martyr actually uses a different wording. It reads: \"POWER: Fanatic deals herself up to 5 Radiant damage. Fanatic deals 1 target X Radiant damage, where X = the amount of Radiant damage dealt to Fanatic this turn.\" Fanatic unambiguously gets both packets boosted separately.</p><p>https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/mr-fixers-dual-crowbars-and-damage-modification</p><p>is the thread if you wanna check it out. There's still wiggle room on how it works with reduction, but the second attack definitely is not double boosted.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:29:00.133Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
